    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n41017" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπίστημα</span></b> , 
			Dor.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπιστέφ-ᾱμα</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ατος</span>, τό, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐφίστημι</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>anything set up</i>, e.g. <i>monument over</i> a grave,
				<i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Lg.</u>
				958e
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Is.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				159
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				12(3).87
			</span></i> (Nisyrus, <span class="entity">iii B.C.</span>), <i><span class="en">
				D.H.
				2.67
			</span></i>; <i>ornament on</i> the prow of ships, <i><span class="en">
				D.S.
				13.3
			</span></i> (nisi leg. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπισήμασι</span>).</div>
